{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/openmpi","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:10.925Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/cbl-mariner/base/openmpi/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/cbl-mariner/base/openmpi/about"},"readme":"***Warning: Azure Linux 2.0 will reach its End of Life (EOL) on July 31st, 2025. After this date, it will no longer receive updates, security patches, or support, which could leave your systems vulnerable. We strongly recommend upgrading to an Azure Linux 3.0 image before July 31st, 2025.***\n\n## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Open MPI image for CBL-Mariner.\n\n### What is CBL-Mariner?\n\nCBL-Mariner is an internal Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. CBL-Mariner is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about CBL-Mariner, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Open MPI?\n\nOpen MPI is a Message Passing Interface (MPI) library project combining technologies and resources from several other projects (FT-MPI, LA-MPI, LAM/MPI, and PACX-MPI.\n\nSee: [Open MPI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/openmpi)\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `4`\n- `4-cm2.0`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to Open MPI version, Mariner build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\nThe Open MPI image ships with a bash shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/openmpi:4\n\n    module load openmpi/gcc\n    mpicc --version\n    \n\n## Support\n\nCBL-Mariner container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe CBL-Mariner distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-07-21T16:48:38.8546997+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"226K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"4.1-cm2.0","digest":"sha256:9931e187ef98be918e90eaabc8d8c8c6d481ea0bc48f90d27e5cf8973b7f3c37","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:58:53.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"4.1","digest":"sha256:9931e187ef98be918e90eaabc8d8c8c6d481ea0bc48f90d27e5cf8973b7f3c37","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:58:42.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"4-cm2.0","digest":"sha256:9931e187ef98be918e90eaabc8d8c8c6d481ea0bc48f90d27e5cf8973b7f3c37","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:58:32.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"4","digest":"sha256:9931e187ef98be918e90eaabc8d8c8c6d481ea0bc48f90d27e5cf8973b7f3c37","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:58:14.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manif